## Why This Is Asked

Observability is critical for CNPA; end-to-end tracing helps identify latency sources across HTTP, DB, and Kafka.

## Key Concepts

- Distributed tracing
- OpenTelemetry SDKs and exporters
- Trace context propagation headers and Kafka headers
- Sampling strategies
- End-to-end verification under load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js OpenTelemetry setup sketch
const tracer = opentelemetry.trace.getTracer('cnpa');
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http', { attributes: { 'http.method': req.method }});
  res.on('finish', () => span.end());
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure producer retries don’t split traces?
- How would you visualize traces and correlate with latency metrics?

## Why This Is Asked
Advanced multi-region CNPA scenarios demand precise fault-localization across HTTP, DB, Kafka, and cross-region replication. This question probes systematic debugging, observability design, and practical fixes that preserve data integrity and latency.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region Kafka replication and lag diagnosis
- End-to-end tracing across services
- Producer batching, acks, and idempotent writes
- Failover testing and impact assessment

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: add a tracing span around HTTP handler to trace end-to-end latency
const tracer = require('@opentelemetry/api');

app.post('/api/events', async (req, res) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http.handle-events');
  try {
    // Business logic here
    await processEvent(req.body);
    res.status(200).json({ success: true });
  } catch (error) {
    span.recordException(error);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Processing failed' });
  } finally {
    span.end();
  }
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
