## Why This Is Asked
This question tests cross-service backpressure handling in CNPA stacks, not just bottleneck triage. It evaluates the ability to design controls that limit upstream load, communicate pressure downstream, and verify effectiveness through realistic load tests.

## Key Concepts
- **Cross-service backpressure**: Coordinated load limiting across API gateway, HTTP handlers, Kafka producers, and Redis clients
- **Per-tenant quotas**: Isolation at the gateway level to prevent noisy neighbor problems
- **In-flight caps and circuit breakers**: Protect downstream services from being overwhelmed
- **Graceful degradation**: Maintain partial functionality during high-load scenarios
- **Observability and threshold design**: Define measurable SLIs for proactive intervention

## Metrics and Thresholds
| Metric | Threshold | Action |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| p95 latency | >500ms | Scale horizontal or enable degradation |
| p99 latency | >1s | Trigger circuit breaker |
| Kafka consumer lag | >10k messages | Pause ingestion or scale consumers |
| Redis queue depth | >1000 | Enable fallback cache |
| In-flight requests | >80% of cap | Reject new requests with 429 |

## Code Example
```javascript
// Per-tenant in-flight limiter
class InFlightLimiter {
  constructor(limit) {
    this.tenantCounts = new Map();
    this.globalCount = 0;
    this.limit = limit;
  }

  allow(tenant) {
    const current = this.tenantCounts.get(tenant) || 0;
    if (current >= this.tenantLimit || this.globalCount >= this.limit) {
      return false;
    }
    this.tenantCounts.set(tenant, current + 1);
    this.globalCount++;
    return true;
  }

  release(tenant) {
    const current = this.tenantCounts.get(tenant) || 0;
    this.tenantCounts.set(tenant, Math.max(0, current - 1));
    this.globalCount = Math.max(0, this.globalCount - 1);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical, end-to-end production-readiness: coupling of writes/reads, cache coherence, and safe rollout in a CNPA stack.

## Key Concepts
- Outbox pattern with idempotent sinks
