## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design safe, minimal, observable feature flag gating in CNPA stacks under concurrency.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and per-request gating
- Centralized flag store vs per-instance cache
- TTL-based cache and cache invalidation
- Canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple gate helper
const FLAG_KEY = 'beta_feature_enabled';
async function isBetaEnabled(redis, cache, ttl = 1000) {
  let v = cache.get(FLAG_KEY);
  if (typeof v !== 'boolean') {
    v = await redis.get(FLAG_KEY);
    cache.set(FLAG_KEY, v, ttl);
  }
  return Boolean(v);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you migrate flags without downtime?
- How would you verify correctness under bursty load?

## Why This Is Asked
Introduces access control in a CNPA stack, a common beginner-friendly area with real-world implications.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC, middleware, JWT validation
- Log redaction and PII protection
- Unit/integration tests, basic load testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-style middleware sketch
function rbac(requiredRoles){
  return (req,res,next)=>{
    const token=req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
    const payload=verifyJwt(token); // assume helper
    if(!payload || !requiredRoles.includes(payload.role)) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
    req.user=payload; next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to support multi-tenant roles?
- How would you test for token revocation and short-lived tokens?
